Let users adjust column widths by dragging header dividers — or double-click to auto-fit. Drag dividers or double-click to auto-fit. This demo saves widths to localStorage. columnResizing onColumnWidthChange to let users drag header dividers. Double-click a handle to auto-fit that column to its content. Column Resizing {RESIZE_PATTERNS.map((pattern) => ( Example Props Enables dragging header dividers to resize columns. Double-click a handle to auto-fit that column to its content. Fires after resize or double-click auto-size with the updated column defs. Use it to persist widths. columnResizing={true} onColumnWidthChange={(headers) => {
  localStorage.setItem(
    "columnWidths",
    JSON.stringify(
      Object.fromEntries(headers.map((h) => [h.accessor, h.width]))
    )
  );
}}

